{{!
    @template local_moodesk/dashboard

    mooDesk Dashboard — the operational support panel.

    Works without JavaScript: every figure is in the markup, and the bars are
    pure CSS.

    Five panels carry data-mhd-chart and are upgraded by dashboard_charts.js
    into a Chart.js rendering — the trend line, the status doughnut, the SLA
    gauge and the priority and aging pies, being the shapes CSS cannot draw
    honestly. Their markup is not removed when that happens: the first three
    move out of sight but stay in the accessibility tree, so the figures remain
    readable as text, and the two pies keep their list on screen as the legend
    that names their slices. Every other panel is CSS by design and stays that
    way.

    Layout follows the reading order an administrator needs: what demands
    attention now (KPIs), whether the backlog is growing (trend + status), how
    urgent and how well-served it is (priority + SLA), where the load sits
    (departments), who is carrying it (workload + aging), what causes it
    (categories), and what just happened (activity).

    Context variables:
      * range_days, range_label - Active window
      * has_any_data            - False when no panel found anything: the panels
                                  give way to a single empty state, while the
                                  KPI row stays, because a count of zero is a
                                  measurement rather than an absence (§8.2)
      * is_manager, is_requester, has_scope, can_filter
      * cansubmit, listurl, submiturl, formaction, clearallurl
      * rangeoptions[]          - {value, label, isselected}
      * departmentoptions[]     - {id, name, isselected}   (+ hasdepartmentoptions)
      * pluginpanels[]          - {html} panels plugins add (+ haspluginpanels), hook dashboard_panels
      * pluginpanelsafterpriority[], pluginpanelsbeforeaging[], pluginpanelsbeforeactivity[]
                                - {html} plugin panels among the base's own
      * pluginfilterselects[]   - {name, label, options[{value, label, isselected}]}
                                  (+ haspluginfilterselects), hook dashboard_filters
      * agentoptions[]          - {id, fullname, isselected} (+ hasagentoptions)
      * chips[]                 - {label, dismissurl}      (+ haschips)
      * hasfilters              - Whether a scope criterion is applied, which is
                                  not the same as haschips: a chip whose label
                                  cannot be resolved is dropped while its
                                  criterion still applies
      * kpis[]                  - {key, label, css_class, icon, note, has_data,
                                   display, no_data_label, has_delta, delta_display,
                                   delta_up, delta_down, delta_label, delta_good,
                                   delta_bad, delta_note}
      * trend                   - {has_data, points[{label, sr_label, created_pct,
                                   resolved_pct}], total_created, total_resolved,
                                   backlog_delta, backlog_rising, no_data_label}
      * status, priority        - {has_data, total, rows[], no_data_label}
      * departments             - {has_data, rows[{label,total,width,segments[]}], legend[]}
      * aging                   - {has_data, total, rows[]}
                                   resolved_total, has_target, target, target_label,
                                   meets_target, breached_label}
      * activity                - {is_available, has_data, rows[]}

    Example context (json):
    {
      "pageheader": {
        "title": "Dashboard",
        "description": null,
        "meta": null,
        "actions": [
          {
            "label": "View all tickets",
            "url": "/local/moodesk/index.php",
            "hasurl": true,
            "icon": null,
            "hasicon": false,
            "icononly": false,
            "variant": "outlined",
            "attributes": [],
            "hasattributes": false
          }
        ],
        "primaryaction": {
          "label": "New ticket",
          "url": "/local/moodesk/submit.php",
          "hasurl": true,
          "icon": "plus",
          "hasicon": true,
          "icononly": true,
          "variant": "filled",
          "attributes": [
            {
              "name": "data-action",
              "value": "mhd-open-new-ticket"
            }
          ],
          "hasattributes": true
        },
        "hasactions": true
      },
      "range_days": 30,
      "range_label": "Last 30 days",
      "has_any_data": true,
      "is_manager": true,
      "can_filter": true,
      "cansubmit": true,
      "listurl": "/local/moodesk/index.php",
      "submiturl": "/local/moodesk/submit.php",
      "formaction": "/local/moodesk/dashboard.php",
      "clearallurl": "/local/moodesk/dashboard.php?days=30",
      "rangeoptions": [{"value": 30, "label": "Last 30 days", "isselected": true}],
      "hasdepartmentoptions": false,
      "hasagentoptions": false,
      "haschips": false,
      "kpis": [
        {"key": "active", "label": "Active tickets", "css_class": "mhd-kpi-blue",
         "icon": "ticket", "note": "Right now", "has_data": true, "display": "25",
         "has_delta": false}
      ],
      "trend": {"has_data": false, "no_data_label": "Not enough data yet"},
      "status": {"has_data": false, "no_data_label": "Not enough data yet"},
      "priority": {"has_data": false, "no_data_label": "Not enough data yet"},
      "departments": {"has_data": false, "no_data_label": "Not enough data yet"},
      "aging": {"has_data": false, "no_data_label": "Not enough data yet"},
      "activity": {"has_data": false, "no_data_label": "Not enough data yet"}
    }
}}
<div class="mhd-dashboard mhd-dashboard--app">

  {{#pageheader}}{{> local_moodesk/page_header }}{{/pageheader}}

  {{! ── Global filters ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      A plain GET form: the whole dashboard state lives in the URL, so it can be
      bookmarked, shared and reloaded. Selects auto-submit where JS is present;
      the Apply button is what makes it work where it is not. }}
  <form class="mhd-filter-bar mhd-dash-filters" method="get" action="{{formaction}}">

    <div class="mhd-filter-select">
      <label class="mhd-filter-label" for="mhd-dash-range">
        {{#str}} dashboard_filter_range, local_moodesk {{/str}}
      </label>
      <select id="mhd-dash-range" name="days" onchange="this.form.submit()">
        {{#rangeoptions}}
        <option value="{{value}}"{{#isselected}} selected{{/isselected}}>{{label}}</option>
        {{/rangeoptions}}
      </select>
    </div>

    {{#can_filter}}

    {{#hasdepartmentoptions}}
    <div class="mhd-filter-select">
      <label class="mhd-filter-label" for="mhd-dash-dept">
        {{#str}} ticket_department, local_moodesk {{/str}}
      </label>
      <select id="mhd-dash-dept" name="departmentid" onchange="this.form.submit()">
        <option value="-1">{{#str}} filter_all_departments, local_moodesk {{/str}}</option>
        <option value="0">{{#str}} dept_none, local_moodesk {{/str}}</option>
        {{#departmentoptions}}
        <option value="{{id}}"{{#isselected}} selected{{/isselected}}>{{name}}</option>
        {{/departmentoptions}}
      </select>
    </div>
    {{/hasdepartmentoptions}}

    {{! Plugin scope filters (hook dashboard_filters) }}
    {{#haspluginfilterselects}}
    {{#pluginfilterselects}}
    <div class="mhd-filter-select">
      <label class="mhd-filter-label" for="mhd-dash-plugin-{{name}}">{{label}}</label>
      <select id="mhd-dash-plugin-{{name}}" name="{{name}}" onchange="this.form.submit()">
        {{#options}}
        <option value="{{value}}"{{#isselected}} selected{{/isselected}}>{{label}}</option>
        {{/options}}
      </select>
    </div>
    {{/pluginfilterselects}}
    {{/haspluginfilterselects}}

    {{#hasagentoptions}}
    <div class="mhd-filter-select">
      <label class="mhd-filter-label" for="mhd-dash-agent">
        {{#str}} dashboard_filter_agent, local_moodesk {{/str}}
      </label>
      <select id="mhd-dash-agent" name="agentid" onchange="this.form.submit()">
        <option value="-1">{{#str}} filter_all_assignees, local_moodesk {{/str}}</option>
        <option value="0">{{#str}} unassigned, local_moodesk {{/str}}</option>
        {{#agentoptions}}
        <option value="{{id}}"{{#isselected}} selected{{/isselected}}>{{fullname}}</option>
        {{/agentoptions}}
      </select>
    </div>
    {{/hasagentoptions}}

    {{/can_filter}}

    <div class="mhd-filter-apply">
      {{! Same call as the ticket list: filtering is not the primary action on
          the page, so it is outlined and Clear all stays the quieter link. }}
      <button type="submit" class="mhd-btn mhd-btn--outlined mhd-btn--xsmall">
        {{#str}} filter_apply, local_moodesk {{/str}}
      </button>
    </div>

    {{#haschips}}
    <a href="{{clearallurl}}" class="mhd-filter-clear-all">
      {{#str}} filter_clear_all, local_moodesk {{/str}}
    </a>
    {{/haschips}}
  </form>

  {{#haschips}}
  <div class="mhd-filter-chips" role="group" aria-label="{{#str}} dashboard_active_filters, local_moodesk {{/str}}">
    {{! Same chip as the ticket list, and now literally the same component:
        components/_pill.scss owns it. The accessible name has to say what
        following the link does — on its own, "Academic Support" is not an
        action. }}
    {{#chips}}
    <a href="{{dismissurl}}"
       class="mhd-pill mhd-pill--input mhd-pill--interactive mhd-pill--trailing-icon"
       aria-label="{{#str}} filter_chip_remove, local_moodesk, {{label}} {{/str}}">
      <span class="mhd-pill__label">{{label}}</span>
      <span class="mhd-pill__icon" aria-hidden="true">&times;</span>
    </a>
    {{/chips}}
  </div>
  {{/haschips}}

  {{! Everything below the filters shares one vertical rhythm, owned by this
      container rather than by each section's own margin — see the SCSS. }}
  <div class="mhd-dash-sections">

  {{! ══ Level 1 — KPIs ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ }}
  <div class="mhd-kpi-grid">
    {{#kpis}}
    <div class="mhd-kpi-card {{css_class}}{{^has_data}} mhd-kpi-card--nodata{{/has_data}}">
      <span class="mhd-kpi-icon" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="#mhd-icon-{{icon}}"></use></svg>
      </span>
      <span class="mhd-kpi-body">
        <span class="mhd-kpi-label">{{label}}</span>
        <span class="mhd-kpi-figure">
          <span class="mhd-kpi-value">{{display}}</span>
          {{#has_delta}}
          {{! Direction and polarity are separate: a rise is not automatically
              good news, so the service decides which of the two colours to use
              — and neither, when the figure did not move at all.

              The arrow is decorative and the colour says nothing to a screen
              reader, so delta_label states the direction in words. }}
          <span class="mhd-kpi-delta{{#delta_good}} mhd-kpi-delta--good{{/delta_good}}{{#delta_bad}} mhd-kpi-delta--bad{{/delta_bad}}">
            <span aria-hidden="true">{{#delta_up}}&uarr;{{/delta_up}}{{#delta_down}}&darr;{{/delta_down}}</span>
            <span class="mhd-sr-only">{{delta_label}}</span>
            {{delta_display}}
          </span>
          {{/has_delta}}
        </span>
        {{^has_data}}
        <span class="mhd-kpi-note mhd-kpi-note--nodata">{{no_data_label}}</span>
        {{/has_data}}
        {{#has_data}}
        <span class="mhd-kpi-note">{{#has_delta}}{{delta_note}}{{/has_delta}}{{^has_delta}}{{note}}{{/has_delta}}</span>
        {{/has_data}}
      </span>
    </div>
    {{/kpis}}
  </div>

  {{! Every panel below is skipped when nothing was found, in favour of saying
      it once. The KPI row above stays: a count of zero is a real measurement
      and worth stating — see docs/dashboard-redesign.md §8.2. }}
  {{#has_any_data}}

  {{! ══ Level 2 — Tickets over time + Tickets by status ═════════════════════ }}

  <section class="mhd-panel mhd-panel--trend mhd-dash-cell mhd-dash-cell--trend" aria-labelledby="mhd-title-trend">
    <header class="mhd-panel-head">
      <h3 class="mhd-panel-title" id="mhd-title-trend">{{#str}} dashboard_section_trend, local_moodesk {{/str}}</h3>
      <span class="mhd-panel-meta">{{range_label}}</span>
    </header>

    {{#trend.has_data}}
    <div class="mhd-trend-legend">
      <span class="mhd-legend-item"><span class="mhd-legend-dot mhd-legend-dot--created"></span>
        {{#str}} dashboard_created, local_moodesk {{/str}} <strong>{{trend.total_created}}</strong></span>
      <span class="mhd-legend-item"><span class="mhd-legend-dot mhd-legend-dot--resolved"></span>
        {{#str}} dashboard_resolved, local_moodesk {{/str}} <strong>{{trend.total_resolved}}</strong></span>
    </div>

    {{! Pure-CSS twin bars, one column per day. dashboard_charts.js draws a
        line chart in front of this and moves it out of sight — but leaves it
        in the accessibility tree, so the figures stay readable as text.

        Which is why each column states its day in words: the bars carry their
        numbers in their height, and a height is not something a screen reader
        can report. Once the canvas mounts, this sentence is the only reading
        of that day left. }}
    <div class="mhd-trend-chart" data-mhd-chart="trend" data-chart-data="{{trend.chart}}">
      {{#trend.points}}
      <div class="mhd-trend-col" title="{{sr_label}}">
        <span class="mhd-sr-only">{{sr_label}}</span>
        <span class="mhd-trend-bar mhd-trend-bar--created" style="height: {{created_pct}}%;" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="mhd-trend-bar mhd-trend-bar--resolved" style="height: {{resolved_pct}}%;" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </div>
      {{/trend.points}}
    </div>

    <p class="mhd-trend-summary{{#trend.backlog_rising}} mhd-trend-summary--warn{{/trend.backlog_rising}}">
      {{#trend.backlog_rising}}
        {{#str}} dashboard_backlog_rising, local_moodesk, {{trend.backlog_delta}} {{/str}}
      {{/trend.backlog_rising}}
      {{^trend.backlog_rising}}
        {{#str}} dashboard_backlog_steady, local_moodesk {{/str}}
      {{/trend.backlog_rising}}
    </p>
    {{/trend.has_data}}

    {{^trend.has_data}}
    <p class="mhd-panel-empty">{{trend.no_data_label}}</p>
    {{/trend.has_data}}
  </section>

  <section class="mhd-panel mhd-panel--status mhd-dash-cell mhd-dash-cell--status" aria-labelledby="mhd-title-status">
    <header class="mhd-panel-head">
      <h3 class="mhd-panel-title" id="mhd-title-status">{{#str}} dashboard_section_status, local_moodesk {{/str}}</h3>
    </header>

    {{#status.has_data}}
    <p class="mhd-panel-total">
      <strong>{{status.total}}</strong> {{#str}} dashboard_active_label, local_moodesk {{/str}}
    </p>
    <ul class="mhd-bd-list" data-mhd-chart="status" data-chart-data="{{status.chart}}">
      {{#status.rows}}
      <li class="mhd-bd-row">
        <span class="mhd-bd-label"><span class="{{css}}"></span>{{label}}</span>
        <span class="mhd-bd-bar" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="mhd-bd-bar-fill" style="width: {{pct}}%;"></span>
        </span>
        <span class="mhd-bd-count">{{count}}</span>
        <span class="mhd-bd-pct">{{pct_display}}</span>
      </li>
      {{/status.rows}}
    </ul>
    {{/status.has_data}}

    {{^status.has_data}}
    <p class="mhd-panel-empty">{{status.no_data_label}}</p>
    {{/status.has_data}}
  </section>

  {{! ══ Level 3 — Tickets by priority, then plugin panels ════════════════════ }}

  <section class="mhd-panel mhd-dash-cell mhd-dash-cell--priority" aria-labelledby="mhd-title-priority">
    <header class="mhd-panel-head">
      <h3 class="mhd-panel-title" id="mhd-title-priority">{{#str}} dashboard_section_priority, local_moodesk {{/str}}</h3>
    </header>

    {{! Unlike the other three charts, this one does not hide the markup it
        replaces: dashboard_charts.js moves the list in beside the pie and
        restyles it as the legend. A pie shows shares but not counts, and its
        slices need naming. }}
    {{#priority.has_data}}
    <ul class="mhd-bd-list" data-mhd-chart="priority" data-chart-data="{{priority.chart}}">
      {{#priority.rows}}
      <li class="mhd-bd-row">
        <span class="mhd-bd-label">{{label}}</span>
        <span class="mhd-bd-bar" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="mhd-bd-bar-fill {{css}}" style="width: {{pct}}%;"></span>
        </span>
        <span class="mhd-bd-count">{{count}}</span>
        <span class="mhd-bd-pct">{{pct_display}}</span>
      </li>
      {{/priority.rows}}
    </ul>
    {{/priority.has_data}}

    {{^priority.has_data}}
    <p class="mhd-panel-empty">{{priority.no_data_label}}</p>
    {{/priority.has_data}}
  </section>

  {{#pluginpanelsafterpriority}}{{{html}}}{{/pluginpanelsafterpriority}}

  {{! ══ Level 4 — Tickets by department ═════════════════════════════════════ }}
  <section class="mhd-panel mhd-dash-cell mhd-dash-cell--dept" aria-labelledby="mhd-title-departments">
    <header class="mhd-panel-head">
      <h3 class="mhd-panel-title" id="mhd-title-departments">{{#str}} dashboard_section_departments, local_moodesk {{/str}}</h3>
    </header>

    {{#departments.has_data}}
    <div class="mhd-dept-legend">
      {{#departments.legend}}
      <span class="mhd-legend-item"><span class="mhd-legend-dot {{css}}"></span>{{label}}</span>
      {{/departments.legend}}
    </div>

    <ul class="mhd-dept-list">
      {{#departments.rows}}
      <li class="mhd-dept-row">
        <span class="mhd-dept-label">{{label}}</span>
        <span class="mhd-dept-bar" style="width: {{width}}%;">
          {{#segments}}
          <span class="mhd-dept-seg {{css}}" style="width: {{pct}}%;"
                title="{{label}}: {{count}}"></span>
          {{/segments}}
        </span>
        <span class="mhd-dept-total">{{total}}</span>
      </li>
      {{/departments.rows}}
    </ul>
    {{/departments.has_data}}

    {{^departments.has_data}}
    <p class="mhd-panel-empty">{{departments.no_data_label}}</p>
    {{/departments.has_data}}
  </section>

  {{! ══ Level 5 — Plugin panels, then Ticket aging ══════════════════════════ }}

  {{#pluginpanelsbeforeaging}}{{{html}}}{{/pluginpanelsbeforeaging}}

  <section class="mhd-panel mhd-panel--aging mhd-dash-cell mhd-dash-cell--aging" aria-labelledby="mhd-title-aging">
    <header class="mhd-panel-head">
      <h3 class="mhd-panel-title" id="mhd-title-aging">{{#str}} dashboard_section_aging, local_moodesk {{/str}}</h3>
      <span class="mhd-panel-meta">{{#str}} dashboard_aging_meta, local_moodesk {{/str}}</span>
    </header>

    {{! Same treatment as priority: the pie replaces the bars, and the list
        stays on as its legend rather than being hidden. }}
    {{#aging.has_data}}
    <ul class="mhd-bd-list" data-mhd-chart="aging" data-chart-data="{{aging.chart}}">
      {{#aging.rows}}
      <li class="mhd-bd-row">
        <span class="mhd-bd-label">{{label}}</span>
        <span class="mhd-bd-bar" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="mhd-bd-bar-fill {{css}}" style="width: {{pct}}%;"></span>
        </span>
        <span class="mhd-bd-count">{{count}}</span>
        <span class="mhd-bd-pct">{{pct_display}}</span>
      </li>
      {{/aging.rows}}
    </ul>
    {{/aging.has_data}}

    {{^aging.has_data}}
    <p class="mhd-panel-empty">{{aging.no_data_label}}</p>
    {{/aging.has_data}}
  </section>

  {{! ══ Level 6 — Plugin panels ════════════════════════════════════════════ }}
  {{#pluginpanelsbeforeactivity}}{{{html}}}{{/pluginpanelsbeforeactivity}}

  {{! ══ Level 7 — Recent activity ═══════════════════════════════════════════ }}
  <section class="mhd-panel mhd-dash-cell mhd-dash-cell--activity" aria-labelledby="mhd-title-activity">
    <header class="mhd-panel-head">
      <h3 class="mhd-panel-title" id="mhd-title-activity">{{#str}} dashboard_section_activity, local_moodesk {{/str}}</h3>
    </header>

    {{#activity.has_data}}
    <ul class="mhd-activity-list">
      {{#activity.rows}}
      <li class="mhd-activity-row">
        <a class="mhd-activity-link" href="{{url}}">
          <span class="mhd-activity-ref">{{ref}}</span>
          <span class="mhd-activity-subject">{{subject}}</span>
        </a>
        <span class="mhd-activity-meta">
          {{#show_priority}}<span class="{{priority_css}}">{{priority}}</span>{{/show_priority}}
          <span class="{{status_css}}">{{status}}</span>
          <span class="mhd-activity-time">{{timeago}}</span>
        </span>
      </li>
      {{/activity.rows}}
    </ul>
    {{/activity.has_data}}

    {{^activity.has_data}}
    <p class="mhd-panel-empty">{{activity.no_data_label}}</p>
    {{/activity.has_data}}
  </section>

  {{/has_any_data}}

  {{! ══ Nothing to show ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════
      Two different facts, and the difference is what the reader needs: a
      filter that excludes everything is recoverable and says how, while a
      quiet period is simply a quiet period. }}
  {{^has_any_data}}
  <section class="mhd-panel mhd-dash-empty">
    <div class="mhd-empty-state">
      <svg class="mhd-empty-state-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <use href="#mhd-icon-tickets"></use>
      </svg>
      {{! Keyed on hasfilters rather than haschips. A chip is dropped when its
          label cannot be resolved — an archived department, a departed agent —
          but the criterion behind it is still applied, and a reader who lands
          on an empty page through one of those needs the way out, not a claim
          that nothing happened this month. }}
      {{#hasfilters}}
      <h3 class="mhd-empty-state-title">{{#str}} dashboard_empty_filtered_title, local_moodesk {{/str}}</h3>
      <p class="mhd-empty-state-desc">{{#str}} dashboard_empty_filtered_body, local_moodesk {{/str}}</p>
      {{! A way back from a filter that matched nothing: recovery, not
          invitation, so outlined rather than filled. }}
      <a href="{{clearallurl}}" class="mhd-btn mhd-btn--outlined">
        {{#str}} filter_clear_all, local_moodesk {{/str}}
      </a>
      {{/hasfilters}}
      {{^hasfilters}}
      <h3 class="mhd-empty-state-title">{{#str}} dashboard_empty_period_title, local_moodesk {{/str}}</h3>
      <p class="mhd-empty-state-desc">{{#str}} dashboard_empty_period_body, local_moodesk {{/str}}</p>
      {{/hasfilters}}
    </div>
  </section>
  {{/has_any_data}}

  {{! Panels plugins add (hook dashboard_panels), whether or not the period had data. }}
  {{#haspluginpanels}}
  {{#pluginpanels}}{{{html}}}{{/pluginpanels}}
  {{/haspluginpanels}}

  </div>{{! /.mhd-dash-sections }}

</div>
